    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive production hinges on a trio of high-efficiency outfielders. **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) leads the charge with an ideal confluence of a weak matchup against Martinez and a favorable park, while **Seiya Suzuki** (75.03) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.72) also cross the 70-point threshold by exploiting porous opposing pitching staffs. **Corbin Carroll** remains a critical start at 67.66 despite a tougher draw against Mize; while we lose some efficiency due to Mize\u2019s ability to hold runners, **Corbin Carroll**'s lead-off slot and elite speed profile make him an essential engine for our stolen base targets. \n\nConversely, we are forced to navigate significant headwinds with our middle infield and corner spots. **Austin Riley** (51.86) is teetering on the edge of viability; while he benefits from a slow delivery that boosts his stolen base potential, his suboptimal batting order spot and a 33% rain risk make him a high-variance play. **Brice Turang** (49.29) faces an uphill battle against the elite arm of Skenes, and while his lead-off role keeps his score afloat, the proximity to a top-tier catcher suppressing his SB upside is a major concern. The decision to bench **Cole Young** (36.38) was the most difficult call of the morning; despite his favorable batting order, the severe SP skill penalty against Anderson and his inability to cross our 40-point efficiency floor necessitated leaving him on the pine. With **James Wood** still sidelined on the IL, we are leaning heavily on **Gabriel Moreno** and **Josh Naylor** to provide stable, if unspectacular, production while our high-ceiling outfielders carry the offensive load.",
